{"name":"Community","hex":"#d0b997","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"community","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A group sharing common characteristics, such as the same language, law, religion, or tradition.","A residential or religious collective; a commune."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community"}],"entries":[{"title":"Community","blocks":[{"text":"A community is a social unit with one or more shared socially-significant characteristics, being place, set of norms, culture, religion, values, customs, or identity. Communities may share a sense of place situated in a given geographical area or in virtual space through communication platforms. Durable good relations that extend beyond immediate genealogical ties also define a sense of community, important to people's identity, practice, and roles in social institutions such as family, home, work, government, society, or humanity at large. Although communities are usually small relative to personal social ties, \"community\" may also refer to large-group affiliations such as national communities, international communities, and virtual communities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Community"},{"title":"Community (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Community is an American television sitcom created by Dan Harmon. The series ran for 110 episodes over six seasons, with its first five seasons airing on NBC from September 17, 2009, to April 17, 2014, and its final season airing on Yahoo Screen from March 17 to June 2, 2015. Set at a community college in the fictional Colorado town of Greendale, the series stars an ensemble cast including Joel McHale, Gillian Jacobs, Danny Pudi, Yvette Nicole Brown, Alison Brie, Donald Glover, Ken Jeong, Chevy Chase, and Jim Rash. It makes use of meta-humor and pop culture references, paying homage to film and television clichés and tropes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Community_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Bigdayout_crowd2.jpg/500px-Bigdayout_crowd2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Bigdayout_crowd2.jpg/500px-Bigdayout_crowd2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"To what extent do participants in joint activities experience a sense of community?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABigdayout_crowd2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Lewes_Bonfire%2C_Martyrs_Crosses.jpg/500px-Lewes_Bonfire%2C_Martyrs_Crosses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Lewes_Bonfire%2C_Martyrs_Crosses.jpg/500px-Lewes_Bonfire%2C_Martyrs_Crosses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lewes Bonfire Night procession commemorating 17 Protestant martyrs burnt at the stake from 1555 to 1557","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALewes_Bonfire%2C_Martyrs_Crosses.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Affinity_group_collateral_damage.jpg/500px-Affinity_group_collateral_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Affinity_group_collateral_damage.jpg/500px-Affinity_group_collateral_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The anti-war affinity group \"Collateral Damage\" protesting the Iraq War","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAffinity_group_collateral_damage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Stonehenge_Summer_Solstice_eve_02.jpg/500px-Stonehenge_Summer_Solstice_eve_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.w